    <string name="about_build">Build</string>
    <string name="about_package">Package</string>
    <string name="about_privacy">Shieldra keeps its evidence encrypted on this phone and sends alerts only through the Telegram bot and email account you set up. It has no server and no account of its own.</string>
    <string name="help_start_title">Get started</string>
    <string name="help_start_body">1. Open Settings, then Protection, and grant the permissions it lists.\n2. Turn on the guards you want: failed unlock, SIM, battery, motion.\n3. Arm protection. Shieldra then guards silently in the background — nothing is shown to whoever holds the phone.</string>
    <string name="help_telegram_title">Telegram alerts</string>
    <string name="help_telegram_body">1. In Telegram open @BotFather, send /newbot and copy the token of your own bot.\n2. Send any message to your new bot, then find your chat ID (for example with @userinfobot).\n3. Paste both in Settings, Alerts &amp; notifications, and tap Test.\n\nTelegram alerts need Shieldra Pro; the free plan sends alerts by email.</string>
    <string name="help_email_title">Email alerts</string>
    <string name="help_email_body">Use your own email account with an app password, not your normal password. In Alerts &amp; notifications choose the server, port and security, enter your address and the app password, then tap Test.</string>
    <string name="help_commands_title">Remote commands</string>
    <string name="help_commands_body">Turn on remote commands in Protection. From your own Telegram chat you can send:\n/locate — current position\n/photo — front-camera photo\n/alarm and /stopalarm\n/track on and /track off — repeating location\n/lost and /found — owner message on the lock screen\n/status — battery and network\n\nRemote commands are part of Shieldra Pro.</string>
    <string name="help_zones_title">Safe zones</string>
    <string name="help_zones_body">On the Map tab, stand in a safe place such as home or work and tap Mark this place as safe, then turn on Alert on leaving. While armed, Shieldra checks the position every few minutes and alerts you when the phone is outside every safe zone.</string>
    <string name="help_export_title">Exporting evidence</string>
    <string name="help_export_body">Open an event and tap Export. Choose a passphrase of 8 or more characters, confirm with your screen lock, and save the encrypted file. Without the passphrase it cannot be opened, so keep it safe.</string>
    <string name="help_battery_title">Keep it running</string>
    <string name="help_battery_body">Allow Shieldra to ignore battery optimisation on the Protection screen and keep the notification permission on, so the guards survive battery saver and a reboot.</string>
    <string name="settings_alerts_and_notifications">Alerts &amp; notifications</string>
    <string name="settings_app_lock_on">On — your screen lock opens Shieldra</string>
    <string name="settings_app_lock_off">Off</string>
    <string name="settings_app_lock_scope">When on, Shieldra opens only with your screen lock — on every launch and when you come back after 30 seconds away. Evidence encryption keys are not tied to it.</string>
