    <string name="settings_privacy">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_collect_title">What Shieldra records</string>
    <string name="privacy_collect_body">Only when a guard you turned on fires, or when you ask from your own Telegram chat: photos from the cameras, a short audio clip, the phone\'s location, and device status such as battery, network and SIM changes. Events and evidence are stored on this phone and evidence files are encrypted with a key that never leaves it.</string>
    <string name="privacy_where_title">Where it can go</string>
    <string name="privacy_where_body">Only to the Telegram bot and the email account that you set up yourself. Shieldra has no server of its own: it does not upload your data to the developer or to anyone else.</string>
    <string name="privacy_never_title">What Shieldra never does</string>
    <string name="privacy_never_body">No analytics, no advertising, no tracking of you, and no selling or sharing of data. Location is read only while protection is armed or when you ask, and goes only to your own channels.</string>
    <string name="privacy_permissions_title">Why it asks for permissions</string>
    <string name="privacy_permissions_body">Camera and microphone: evidence after an incident. Location: where the phone is. Device administrator: to notice failed unlock attempts. Notifications: to keep protection running and show alerts. Screen lock: to confirm it is you for export, deletion and app lock.</string>
    <string name="privacy_billing_title">Shieldra Pro</string>
    <string name="privacy_billing_body">Payment is handled by Google Play. Shieldra only learns whether you own Pro; it never sees your card or account details.</string>
    <string name="privacy_control_title">Your control</string>
    <string name="privacy_control_body">Export evidence as an encrypted file, delete it automatically after 90 days (events) and 30 days (evidence), lock the app with your screen lock, or delete all data now in Settings. Uninstalling Shieldra removes everything it stored.</string>
    <string name="erase_title">Delete all data?</string>
    <string name="erase_body">This permanently deletes every recorded event and every evidence file on this phone, and destroys the keys that open them. It cannot be undone. Your alert channels and settings stay. Shieldra restarts afterwards.</string>
